# Project architecture

## Stack (do not change major versions)

- PHP 8.4, Laravel 11 (locked 11.57.1). Do not use Laravel 12/13-only APIs.
- stancl/tenancy `^3.8` (locked 3.10.1), multi-database, tenants identified by domain.
- Inertia 2 + React 18 in plain JSX (no TypeScript), Breeze scaffolding, Tailwind 3, Vite 5.
- PHPUnit 10 (not Pest). MySQL 8.0+ locally; SQLite `:memory:` in tests.

## Where things live

- Central routes: `routes/web.php`, wrapped in `Route::domain('{centralDomain}')`.
  Central domains are listed in `config/tenancy.php` (`127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, `blogs.test`, `platform.test`).
- Tenant routes: `routes/tenant.php`, middleware order
  `web`, `InitializeTenancyByDomain`, `PreventAccessFromCentralDomains`, `ScopeSessions`, `EnsureTenantIsActive`, `UseWriterGuard`.
- Tenant writer routes for `posts/{post}` use `->whereNumber('post')` so the public
  `posts/{slug}` route (`blog.show`) stays reachable. Keep that ordering and constraint.
- Central models: `App\Models\Tenant`, `App\Models\User`, `App\Models\Domain` (extends stancl's, adds `is_primary`;
  set as `tenancy.domain_model`), `App\Models\AuditLog`, stancl `ImpersonationToken`.
- Tenant models: `App\Models\Writer` (table `users`, `role` is `TenantUserRole`: `admin` or `writer`), `App\Models\Post`,
  `Contact`, `Tag`, `ContactNote`, and `ContactImport`. All of them throw if tenancy is not initialized.
- Tenant-aware helpers: `app/Support/TenantCoverImage.php`, `TenantBranding.php`, `HomepageCache.php`.
- Tenant lifecycle: `app/Support/TenantLifecycle.php` (`provision()` with rollback, `delete()` through the stancl pipeline).
  Domain validation and normalization: `app/Support/DomainName.php`. Use `$tenant->primaryDomainName()`, never `domains->first()`.
- Central authorization: every central ability lives in `app/Support/CentralAbility.php` and is enforced with `can:` route
  middleware. Support is read-only plus impersonation of non-admin writers (`CentralAbility::canImpersonate`).
- Tenant authorization: `app/Support/TenantAbility.php`, checked against the `writer` guard and only while tenancy is
  initialized. Post access stays in `PostPolicy` and `Post::scopeVisibleToWriter()`. Tenant admins manage users at
  `/writers` (`Writer\UserController`). `role` stays off `Writer::$fillable` and is set with `forceFill`.
- Impersonation: `Admin\ImpersonationController` issues a stancl `ImpersonationToken` and POSTs it (never in a URL) to the
  tenant's `/impersonate` route (`Writer\ImpersonationController`), which consumes it atomically. Session state is in
  `app/Support/Impersonation.php`. A tenant admin impersonates a writer in the same tenant through
  `TenantImpersonation` (`tenant_impersonation` session key, `POST /writers/{writer}/impersonate`). Do not store a
  tenant writer id in `audit_logs.actor_id`. Audit every start, stop and admin mutation with `AuditLog::record()`.
- Contacts: tenant routes under `can:tenant.manage-contacts`. Each contact has an `owner_id` and optional rows in
  `contact_shares`. Tenant admins see every contact; other users see contacts they own or that are shared with them.
  CSV import is `ImportContacts`, which re-initializes the tenant id captured when the job was dispatched and assigns
  the uploading user as owner. Files stay on the tenant disk.
- Scheduled publishing: `app/Console/Commands/PublishDuePosts.php` (`posts:publish-due`, every minute in
  `routes/console.php`) and `app/Jobs/PublishScheduledPost.php`.
- Pages: `resources/js/Pages/{Admin,Writer,Blog}`; layouts in `resources/js/Layouts`.

## Conventions

- Validate in Form Requests (`app/Http/Requests`), authorize with policies (`PostPolicy` is
  registered in `AppServiceProvider` via `Gate::policy`).
- Vite assets use `global_asset()` (set in `AppServiceProvider`) so tenant domains load `/build` correctly.
- Prefer extending existing helpers over adding parallel ones.
